%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7c7c947f0ccabb24dbf991df8e9f6d4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: district level agencies
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  defaultQuestions:
  - QuestionText: Which institution is the nodal agency for in-service teacher education
      at the elementary level in a district?
    Options:
    - SCERT
    - DIET
    - NCERT
    - UGC
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The CRC (Cluster Resource Centre) typically caters to a group
      of:'
    Options:
    - All schools in a state
    - 10-15 schools in a geographical cluster
    - Only private schools in a district
    - Secondary schools only
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The primary function of a Block Resource Centre (BRC) is to:'
    Options:
    - Develop national curriculum frameworks
    - Provide academic support and training to teachers at the block level
    - Regulate university education
    - Manage district finances
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: Who acts as the direct mentor and academic guide for teachers at
      the cluster level?
    Options:
    - The District Collector
    - The DIET Principal
    - The CRC Coordinator
    - The School Principal
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The administrative head responsible for coordinating all in-service
      training programs in a district is the:'
    Options:
    - DIET Lecturer
    - District Education Officer (DEO)
    - CRC Coordinator
    - BRC Coordinator
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a key role of a DIET?
    Options:
    - Awarding Ph.D. degrees
    - Developing locally relevant Teaching-Learning Materials (TLMs)
    - Setting national education policy
    - Governing higher education institutions
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The institutional structure for in-service teacher education at
      the district level follows a cascade model. The correct sequence is:'
    Options:
    - NCERT -> SCERT -> DIET -> BRC -> CRC
    - CRC -> BRC -> DIET -> SCERT -> NCERT
    - UGC -> DIET -> CRC -> Teacher
    - School -> State -> National -> International
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher facing a classroom challenge would first seek on-site
      academic support from the:'
    Options:
    - NCERT
    - SCERT
    - CRC Coordinator
    - University Professor
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: The main target group for DIET's in-service programs are teachers
      of which level?
    Options:
    - Higher Education
    - Secondary and Senior Secondary
    - Elementary Education (Classes I-VIII)
    - Pre-primary only
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which agency is responsible for the logistical arrangements for
      a large-scale district-level teacher training workshop?
    Options:
    - DIET
    - District Education Office (DEO)
    - CRC
    - State Government Secretariat
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The "C" in CRC stands for:'
    Options:
    - Central
    - Cluster
    - Core
    - Curriculum
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A BRC Coordinator receives academic guidance and resources primarily
      from the:'
    Options:
    - State Education Minister
    - DIET
    - University Grants Commission
    - Central Board of Secondary Education
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which institution is most directly involved in organizing monthly
      cluster-level meetings for teachers?
    Options:
    - DIET
    - BRC
    - CRC
    - SCERT
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The primary purpose of establishing a multi-level structure (DIET,
      BRC, CRC) is to:'
    Options:
    - Increase bureaucratic hurdles
    - Ensure academic support reaches every single teacher
    - Reduce the number of training programs
    - Centralize all decision-making
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A DIET also plays a significant role in the training of:'
    Options:
    - Corporate managers
    - Headteachers and school principals
    - Medical doctors
    - Engineering students
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is NOT typically a function of a DIET?
    Options:
    - Conducting action research on local educational problems
    - Organizing cultural festivals for the public
    - Providing in-service training to elementary teachers
    - Acting as a resource centre for the district
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The success of the CRC model heavily relies on the:'
    Options:
    - Political affiliation of the coordinator
    - Weather conditions in the district
    - Number of schools in the state
    - Proactive and supportive role of the CRC Coordinator
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher seeking a transfer within the district for professional
      development would approach the:'
    Options:
    - CRC Coordinator
    - District Education Officer (DEO)
    - School Principal
    - Block Development Officer
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The institution that serves as the academic backbone of the Sarva
      Shiksha Abhiyan (SSA) at the district level is the:'
    Options:
    - District Court
    - DIET
    - Local College
    - Police Station
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which agency is responsible for identifying master trainers at
      the district level who can then train other teachers?
    Options:
    - SCERT
    - NCERT
    - CRC
    - DIET
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A "Resource Centre" at the district level, where teachers can
      access books, journals, and TLMs, is typically located at the:'
    Options:
    - District Library
    - DIET
    - Zilla Panchayat Office
    - State Secretariat
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The "B" in BRC stands for:'
    Options:
    - Basic
    - Block
    - Board
    - Bureau
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The primary focus of in-service training at the CRC level is:'
    Options:
    - High-level theoretical research
    - Administrative law
    - International educational policies
    - Immediate, practical classroom-based issues
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which of the following agencies is most likely to conduct a training
      program on a new state textbook for all language teachers in a block?
    Options:
    - NCERT
    - BRC
    - UGC
    - AICTE
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: The creation of DIETs was a major recommendation of which national
      policy?
    Options:
    - National Policy on Education (NPE), 1986
    - National Curriculum Framework (NCF), 2005
    - Kothari Commission (1964-66)
    - Right to Education Act (RTE), 2009
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A key challenge faced by district-level agencies is:'
    Options:
    - Lack of any teachers to train
    - Inadequate infrastructure and funding for effective training
    - Over-qualification of all teachers
    - Absence of a national curriculum
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The role of the District Education Officer (DEO) in in-service
      education is primarily:'
    Options:
    - Academic and pedagogical
    - Administrative and supervisory
    - Financial auditing of schools
    - Teaching students directly
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which institution would be responsible for training Key Resource
      Persons (KRPs) who will then train teachers at the block and cluster level?
    Options:
    - CRC
    - BRC
    - DIET
    - SCERT
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The main advantage of having a CRC is that it provides:'
    Options:
    - A centralized location for all state-level policy making
    - Localized, context-specific, and accessible support to teachers
    - A platform for political campaigns
    - Free meals for teachers
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A DIET is established in every district by the:'
    Options:
    - Central Government alone
    - State Government
    - United Nations
    - Private corporations
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which agency is responsible for monitoring the academic progress
      of schools within a cluster?
    Options:
    - DIET
    - NCTE
    - NCERT
    - CRC
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The "I" in DIET stands for:'
    Options:
    - International
    - Institute
    - Indian
    - Integrated
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher wishing to access digital resources for teaching science
      would most likely be directed to the resource centre at the:'
    Options:
    - BRC or DIET
    - District Court
    - Local Market
    - State Capital
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The cascade model of training, implemented through DIETs, BRCs,
      and CRCs, is often criticized for:'
    Options:
    - Being too fast and efficient
    - Dilution of training quality as it trickles down
    - Involving too few people
    - Being too expensive for the government
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which district-level institution is most directly involved in the
      "on-the-job" support of a teacher?
    Options:
    - DIET
    - CRC
    - District Treasury
    - State SCERT
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The primary source of funding for the functioning of DIETs, BRCs,
      and CRCs is the:'
    Options:
    - Central Government (through schemes like Samagra Shiksha)
    - Local community donations
    - Student fees
    - International aid
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A program aimed at training all mathematics teachers in a district
      on a new pedagogical approach would be organized by the:'
    Options:
    - CRC
    - DIET in coordination with BRCs/CRCs
    - Individual schools independently
    - National Testing Agency
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The institution that maintains records of teacher attendance and
      leave at the district level is the:'
    Options:
    - DIET
    - District Education Office (DEO)
    - CRC
    - BRC
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The "E" in DIET stands for:'
    Options:
    - Economic
    - Emergency
    - Environmental
    - Elementary
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A major function of the BRC is to:'
    Options:
    - Award graduate degrees
    - Act as a bridge between the DIET and the CRCs
    - Set national educational standards
    - Manage the state's education budget
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a correct statement about the relationship
      between these agencies?
    Options:
    - The CRC reports to the BRC, which reports to the DIET.
    - The DIET reports to the CRC, which reports to the BRC.
    - The BRC and CRC are independent of each other.
    - The NCERT directly manages all CRCs.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'For a secondary school teacher, in-service training at the district
      level might also be provided by a:'
    Options:
    - College of Teacher Education (CTE)
    - Primary Health Centre
    - Anganwadi worker
    - Traffic Police department
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The ultimate goal of all these district-level agencies is to:'
    Options:
    - Increase the administrative workload of teachers
    - Improve the quality of classroom transactions and student learning
    - Create more government jobs
    - Reduce the number of schools
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A "Master Trainer" identified by the DIET is responsible for:'
    Options:
    - Training other teachers in their area of expertise
    - Managing the district's sports events
    - Cooking meals for mid-day meals
    - Driving the school bus
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The district-level structure for in-service education is a key
      component of:'
    Options:
    - The national defense strategy
    - India's efforts to achieve Universalization of Elementary Education (UEE)
    - The foreign policy of India
    - The industrial development plan
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A workshop on "Continuous and Comprehensive Evaluation (CCE)"
      for all teachers in a block would be organized by the:'
    Options:
    - BRC
    - National Commission for Minorities
    - Supreme Court of India
    - Reserve Bank of India
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The academic authority that provides the broad framework and guidelines
      for the training conducted by DIETs is the:'
    Options:
    - SCERT
    - CRC
    - Local Municipal Corporation
    - District Police
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A significant challenge for CRC Coordinators is:'
    Options:
    - Having too few teachers to support
    - The large number of schools and diverse needs they have to cater to
    - The absence of any defined role
    - Being overpaid for their work
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The "T" in DIET stands for:'
    Options:
    - Technology
    - Terminal
    - Tertiary
    - Training
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: district level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The effectiveness of the entire district-level support system
      is most visible in the:'
    Options:
    - Number of meetings held
    - Improved teaching practices and student outcomes in classrooms
    - Size of the government office buildings
    - Number of cars owned by officials
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: district level agencies
